I haven't added `aap:caps/http-client`. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0`, and that clause is its entire authority. A change to the grant belongs in the graph definition, not in the node body, so the world below imports only `state-read`. Once you update the graph's `with` clause, the http-client import and enrichment call can be added. The `RunInfo` input also has no text field, so the enrichment query would need a defined source for its `q` value.

I read the subscription list from state key `"urls"`, one URL per line. Blank lines are dropped, and a missing key yields an empty list.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{run-info, subscription-list};

    import aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(info: run-info) -> subscription-list;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use aap::caps::state_read;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(_info: RunInfo) -> SubscriptionList {
        let urls = match state_read::get("urls") {
            Some(raw) => raw
                .lines()
                .map(str::trim)
                .filter(|line| !line.is_empty())
                .map(String::from)
                .collect(),
            None => Vec::new(),
        };
        SubscriptionList { urls }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

